>In article <kkittyCqzoL4.MBq@netcom.com> you wrote:

>:  One collar seems like it would be more than enough, though limiting a 
>: collar by making it limited to a specific pet type. ie. a small dog 
>: collar will not work for a large dog, or for your pet purple worm or (though 
>: I guess it would be strange wandering around and finding a grey dragon 
>: collar)

>And when your pet gets polymorphed, he breaks his collar, or chokes on
>it (leather or chain collars), or it pops over his head (pet gets
>smaller).

I think that, perhaps, one of two methods should be used for collar sizing.

1) The collars come in small, medium, and large, and each size fits various
critter types. ie your "little dog" gets a small collar, while your "black
dragon" gets a large.

or,
2) The collars magically size themselves, like rings and amulets do. Doggie
armor should break apart upon polymorphing, like human armor does (of course,
it could weld itself to the pet like scale armor does; Imagine having your
little dog in doggie grey dragon scale mail getting polymorphed into a grey
dragon! ooo...), but rings and amulets usually stay with a human "You have a
ring of invisibility on your right forepaw", and so should collars.

